# Project Overview
This repository documents a comprehensive, hands-on network security lab simulating real-world defensive and offensive operations. The lab covers active network scanning, firewall behavior analysis (DROP vs. REJECT), Public Key Infrastructure (PKI) concepts, and a complete simulation of a state-of-the-art **TLS 1.3 Handshake** using OpenSSL and Wireshark.

###  Lab Architecture
*   **Attacker/Client Node:** Kali Linux (`10.10.10.X`)
*   **Target/Server Node:** Ubuntu Server (`10.10.10.20`)
*   **Network Analyzer:** Wireshark Packet Sniffer
*   **Security Boundary:** Uncomplicated Firewall (UFW) on Ubuntu
