Core Takeaways
Stealth vs. Noise: SYN scans bypass basic application-level logging but are easily flagged by network-level Intrusion Detection Systems (IDS).
Defensive Firewalling: Utilizing a DROP policy on firewalls increases the time and resources required for attackers to map an attack surface.
TLS 1.3 Efficiency: TLS 1.3 provides a massive performance upgrade (1-RTT handshake) and enhanced privacy by encrypting handshake metadata (certificates) that TLS 1.2 left in cleartext.
Zero-Trust Encryption: Even with physical access to the network medium (simulated by Wireshark), data remains completely secure if robust, modern symmetric algorithms (AES-GCM) are correctly implemented. ```



